cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "JABD — Job Advertisements Bias Dataset"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the dataset and the accompanying paper."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A token-level, human-annotated corpus for studying linguistic bias in job
  advertisements. 14,960 sentences drawn from 8,993 real postings, annotated
  under a four-level taxonomy separating explicit from implicit bias across five
  sociodemographic groups (gender, ethnicity, age, religion, disability), with
  34,598 flagged spans over 12 leaf classes. Released as the annotation layer
  only; the source advertisement text is not redistributed.
